{"tool_name":"rppocket","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rppocket","home":"http://zhaoserver.com.cn/RPpocket/RPpocket.html","summary":"An RNA-Protein Intuitive Database with RNA Pocket Topology Resources.","addition_date":"2022-09-28T20:20:23.282422Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:33:57.166986Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:rppocket","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"yjzhaowh@mail.ccnu.edu.cn","name":"Yunjie Zhao","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Haoquan Liu"},{"name":"Liu Yang"},{"name":"Rui Yang"},{"name":"Ting Zhou"},{"name":"Xinyao Li"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0267"},{"term":"RNA binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3902"},{"term":"RNA secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0278"},{"term":"Structural motif discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0245"},{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}]}],"name":"RPpocket","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.3390/ijms23136903","metadata":{"abstract":"RNA\u2013protein complexes regulate a variety of biological functions. Thus, it is essential to explore and visualize RNA\u2013protein structural interaction features, especially pocket interactions. In this work, we develop an easy\u2010to\u2010use bioinformatics resource: RPpocket. This database provides RNA\u2013protein complex interactions based on sequence, secondary structure, and pocket topology analysis. We extracted 793 pockets from 74 non\u2010redundant RNA\u2013protein structures. Then, we calculated the binding\u2010 and non\u2010binding pocket topological properties and analyzed the binding mechanism of the RNA\u2013protein complex. The results showed that the binding pockets were more extended than the non\u2010binding pockets. We also found that long\u2010range forces were the main interaction for RNA\u2013protein recognition, while short\u2010range forces strengthened and optimized the binding. RPpocket could facilitate RNA\u2013protein engineering for biological or medical applications.","authors":[{"name":"Li X."},{"name":"Liu H."},{"name":"Yang L."},{"name":"Yang R."},{"name":"Zhao Y."},{"name":"Zhou T."}],"citationCount":4,"date":"2022-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","title":"RPpocket: An RNA\u2013Protein Intuitive Database with RNA Pocket Topology Resources"},"pmcid":"PMC9266927","pmid":"35805909"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Molecular modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2275"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"RPpocket","home":"https://bio.tools/rppocket","summary":"An RNA-Protein Intuitive Database with RNA Pocket Topology Resources.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rppocket/db/zhaoserver.com.cn","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":7,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.3390/ijms23136903","pmcid":"PMC9266927","pmid":"35805909","ref_count":48,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1971"},{"count":1,"year":"1977"},{"count":1,"year":"1979"},{"count":1,"year":"1995"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"}